<title>MEXICO: Mexican pension funds sign up 3.779 mln workers.</title>
<headline>Mexican pension funds sign up 3.779 mln workers.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Some 3.779 million workers had joined one of 17 pension fund management firms (Afore) by June 6, with Afore Bancomer remaining the most popular, the National Retirement Savings System Commission said on Monday.</p>
<p>It issued the following list detailing total affiliations and market share of each Afore.</p>
<p>   Afore		   Total   Market share (%)</p>
<p>-------------------------------------</p>
<p>   Bancomer		880,044     23.28</p>
<p>   Banamex		 677,954     17.94</p>
<p>   Santander-Mexicano  534,09	14.13</p>
<p>   Profuturo-GNP	 448,552     11.87</p>
<p>   Bital		   441,959     11.69</p>
<p>   Garante		 267,349	7.07</p>
<p>   Banorte		 212,217	5.61</p>
<p>   Bancrecer-Dresdner  105,245	2.78</p>
<p>   Previnter		71,097	1.88</p>
<p>   Inbursa		  45,030	1.19</p>
<p>   Atlantico-Promex     42,279	1.12</p>
<p>   Genesis		  19,161	0.51</p>
<p>   Afore XXI		 9,779	0.26</p>
<p>   Tepeyac		   8,707	0.23</p>
<p>   Zurich		    7,736	0.20</p>
<p>   Confa-Principal	7,527	0.20</p>
<p>   Capitaliza		1,040	0.03</p>
<p>--------------------------------------</p>
<p>   TOTAL		 3,779,766    100.00</p>
<p>((--Cyntia Barrera Diaz, Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9549))</p>
</text>
